Upgrade procedure for libarchive

Source: https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive (signed tags vVERSION;
	releases are tagged by Martin Matuska,
	659C84C0E23EA1FA97E0B58CC040B508D63D2B36)

The vendor branch (vendor/libarchive/dist) carries the complete upstream
tree at the release tag, including .github/ and other files that
.gitignore would hide.  Pruning happens only in contrib/libarchive.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Check out the tag and verify its signature:
	git clone https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive.git
	git -C libarchive tag -v vVERSION
   Export the tree with "git --work-tree=DIR checkout vVERSION -- ."
   rather than "git archive", which drops export-ignore'd files.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/libarchive/dist,
   contrib/libarchive, tag vendor/libarchive/dist/VERSION).  Stage with
   "git add -A -f" so files matched by upstream's .gitignore are kept,
   and check that the staged tree equals the upstream tag's tree.
3. Merge.  libarchive 3.8.8 reached master as a squash merge (PR #451),
   so its vendor commit is not an ancestor of master and a plain
   "git merge -Xsubtree" uses 3.8.7 as the base.  Once a real merge of
   3.8.11 or later is on the branch this no longer matters.
4. Resolve:
   - Files that upstream changed but that are pruned in-tree show up as
     modify/delete conflicts; git rm them.
   - New upstream files in pruned areas (CI, CMake, build/, contrib/,
     examples/, Windows resources and ports) are added by the merge;
     git rm them as well.  See MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist.
5. Update the build glue:
   - lib/libarchive/Makefile, usr.bin/{tar,cpio,bsdcat,unzip}/Makefile:
     new sources.
   - lib/libarchive/config_midnightbsd.h: new HAVE_* macros.  Compare
     with FreeBSD's lib/libarchive/config_freebsd.h, and only define
     functions MidnightBSD has (memset_explicit is missing, for
     example).
   - lib/libarchive/tests/Makefile and usr.bin/*/tests/Makefile list
     every test source and .uu file; add the new ones.  FreeBSD's test
     Makefiles are a good reference.
6. Build lib/libarchive, the four programs and their tests, and run the
   test programs (libarchive_test -r contrib/libarchive/libarchive/test,
   bsdtar_test -p bsdtar -r contrib/libarchive/tar/test, and so on).
   test_write_disk fails when run as root; run it as an unprivileged
   user.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - test_utils/test_common.h: include config_midnightbsd.h when building
    on MidnightBSD (only used without PLATFORM_CONFIG_H).
  - libarchive/test/test_write_format_pax_align.c: rename the ALIGN
    macro to PAX_ALIGN; ALIGN clashes with <machine/param.h>
    (FreeBSD 47f89e7907e2).
  - libarchive/archive_write_disk_posix.c: ssize_t for the
    extattr_set_*() result in set_xattrs().
  - libarchive/archive_write_set_format_7zip.c: "unsigned int" for a
    bit-field.
  - libarchive/test/test_extattr_freebsd.c: ssize_t for the extattr
    call results.
  - libarchive/archive_entry.c, archive_read_support_filter_compress.c:
    BSD license clause renumbered (3 instead of 4).
  - libarchive/test/test_read_format_gtar_sparse_skip_entry.c: FreeBSD
    backport guard.
  - libarchive/test/main.c: an old copy of the test harness, left over
    from before 3.7.7.  It is not built (the tests use
    test_utils/test_main.c) and could be removed.
  - Small differences in test_read_format_mtree.mtree.uu,
    test_read_format_zip.zip.uu, test_read_format_lha_oversize_header.c
    and libarchive_fe/line_reader.h ($FreeBSD$ lines).

  Dropped in 3.8.11: the archive_string.c change that made the
  FreeBSD-only iconvctl(ICONV_SET_ILSEQ_INVALID) block apply to
  MidnightBSD.  Upstream removed that block because libarchive now
  handles POSIX iconv semantics (upstream PR #3531).
